--TEST--
`Core\Http\Client::patch` cannot ask for retries without `retryIdempotencyKey`, and the key is what makes the retry legal — `rule:http-server/a-non-idempotent-retry-needs-an-idempotency-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:http-server/a-non-idempotent-retry-needs-an-idempotency-key`: a `PATCH`
// applies a change rather than restating one, so a repeated attempt is a second
// effect and needs an identity the server can recognise — the same obligation
// `POST` carries, asked here of the other verb on that roster. Both halves of
// the question are written at the call — the verb is the member's own name, and
// `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2 makes the bag a literal — so it is refused
// while compiling, and no request is made to discover it.
string $url = "https://example.test/orders/7";

var $a = Core\Http\Client::patch($url, {json: ["status" => "paid"], retryAttempts: 3});

// The bound on its other side, so a refusal written one condition too wide
// fails here: the key makes the same retry legal, and a `patch` that asks for
// no retry owes no key at all.
var $b = Core\Http\Client::patch($url, {json: ["status" => "paid"], retryAttempts: 3, retryIdempotencyKey: "order-7"});
var $c = Core\Http\Client::patch($url, {json: ["status" => "paid"]});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0796]: `Core\Http\Client::patch` asks for retries without `retryIdempotencyKey`
   --> case.nvs:11:69
%A
   = help: a repeated `PATCH` is a second effect rather than a second question, so an attempt needs an identity the server can recognise: add `retryIdempotencyKey: "..."` to the same bag, sent as `Idempotency-Key` and identical across attempts
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
